"test":{"name":"fog-ai-knowledge","kind":"rules","opponent":"Human","rounds":"4","check":"fogKnowledge","question":"The AI playing by the fog: thinking, it knows only what Blue sees — a hidden enemy is off the board (not in its read of the board, not targetable, not blocking) and one seen lately stands where it was last seen, unless that tile is in sight and empty; everything is put back afterwards. An ambush tile (out of the enemy's sight, in reach of an enemy) is worth something, an exposed one is not; a stop that brings unseen tiles into sight is worth more than one that does not. With fogFair off it knows everything.","rules":"attrition","fog":"on"},
